`crimes context src/Card.tsx` confirms medium overall risk: one accessibility hazard and two low-risk styling findings. It also found no related tests, so the refactor should include focused component coverage.

I’d replace the clickable card container with a semantic card plus an explicit action:

```tsx
import styles from "./Card.module.css";

type CardProps = {
  children: React.ReactNode;
  onActivate: () => void;
};

export function Card({ children, onActivate }: CardProps) {
  return (
    <article className={styles.card}>
      <div className={styles.layout}>
        <div className={styles.content}>{children}</div>
        <aside className={styles.sidebar}>sidebar</aside>
      </div>

      <button type="button" className={styles.action} onClick={onActivate}>
        Open details
      </button>
    </article>
  );
}
```

The accompanying CSS should:

```css
.card {
  container-type: inline-size;
  inline-size: 100%;
  max-inline-size: var(--size-content-lg);
  padding: var(--space-6);
  background: var(--color-surface);
  color: var(--color-ink);
  border: var(--border-default);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
}

.layout {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: var(--space-4);
}

.content {
  min-inline-size: 0;
  font-size: clamp(
    var(--font-size-md),
    var(--font-size-fluid),
    var(--font-size-lg)
  );
}

.sidebar {
  color: var(--color-ink-muted);
}

.action:focus-visible {
  outline: var(--focus-ring);
  outline-offset: var(--space-1);
}

@container (min-width: 40rem) {
  .layout {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) var(--size-sidebar);
  }
}
```

How each finding is addressed:

- `accessible_interaction_risk`: removes `onClick` from the `<div>` and exposes a native `<button>` with visible text. Keyboard activation, focus, and screen-reader semantics work without manually reproducing button behavior with ARIA.
- `design_token_escape`: replaces inline hex, RGB, pixel, and shadow literals with semantic design-system tokens. Existing `surface`, `ink`, and `brand` values in [tailwind.config.ts](/Users/andrew/dev/crimes/evals/fixtures/07-stress-frontend/tailwind.config.ts) can back these tokens; missing muted-text, border, shadow, sizing, and focus tokens should be added centrally.
- `responsive_fragility`: removes the fixed `800px`/`720px` widths and `600px` height, uses fluid inline sizing, prevents grid overflow with `minmax(0, 1fr)`, scales typography with `clamp()`, and introduces the sidebar only when the card’s own container has enough space.

Because context reported no likely tests, I’d add a `Card.test.tsx` covering keyboard activation and accessible naming, plus narrow/wide container rendering. If preserving “click anywhere on the card” is mandatory, the root can instead be a `<button>`, but only if `children` are guaranteed never to contain links, controls, or other interactive elements.
